id: PCL:0113061
name: Sncg Gaba_5 Evc sncg GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A sncg GABAergic cortical interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Krt73 (Mmus), Vip (Mmus), Slc17a8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Sncg Gaba_5 cells by expression of Evc, Stk32b. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Hippocampal region, Cortical subplate, in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, Field CA3, stratum oriens, Posterior amygdalar nucleus, Field CA1, stratum radiatum, Field CA3, pyramidal layer, Field CA3, stratum radiatum. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:0681 Sncg Gaba_5 (CS20230722_CLUS_0681)." []
