[Term]
id: PCL:0113063
name: Sncg Gaba_7 sncg GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A sncg GABAergic cortical interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Krt73 (Mmus), Pax6 (Mmus), Fmo1 (Mmus), Htr3a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Sncg Gaba cells by expression of Ccdc141, Col14a1, Krt73. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Isocortex, in or close to the regions: Primary motor area, Layer 1, Supplemental somatosensory area, layer 1, Primary somatosensory area, mouth, layer 1, Agranular insular area, dorsal part, layer 1. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:0683 Sncg Gaba_7 (CS20230722_SUPT_0191, CS20230722_CLUS_0683)." []
