[Term]
id: PCL:0113066
name: RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_1 Ecel1 caudal ganglionic eminence derived cortical interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A caudal ganglionic eminence derived cortical interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Rarres1 (Mmus), Syt6 (Mmus), Gm31218 (Mmus), Npy2r (Mmus). It is distinguished from other RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_1 cells by expression of Ecel1, Rarres1. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Hippocampal region, Retrohippocampal region, in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum lacunosum-moleculare, Field CA1, stratum radiatum, Field CA3, pyramidal layer, Field CA3, stratum radiatum, Dentate gyrus, molecular layer, Field CA3, stratum lacunosum-moleculare. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:0686 RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_0686)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_1 Ecel1 does not have cells in cortical amygdalar area (COA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0686 RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_1" EXACT []
