[Term]
id: PCL:0113077
name: RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_4 Sytl4 caudal ganglionic eminence derived cortical interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A caudal ganglionic eminence derived cortical interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Sln (Mmus), Sytl4 (Mmus), Gas2l3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_4 cells by expression of Sytl4, Gas2l3. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Hippocampal region, in or close to the regions: Field CA1, stratum oriens, Field CA3, stratum oriens, Field CA1, stratum radiatum, Field CA3, pyramidal layer, Field CA3, stratum radiatum, Field CA1, pyramidal layer. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:0697 RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_4 (CS20230722_CLUS_0697)." []
comment: Warning: This type RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_4 Sytl4 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for retrohippocampal region (RHP), cortical amygdalar area (COA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "0697 RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_4" EXACT []
