[Term]
id: PCL:0113079
name: RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_5 Snx31 caudal ganglionic eminence derived cortical interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A caudal ganglionic eminence derived cortical interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Snx31 (Mmus), Prok2 (Mmus), Lin7a (Mmus), Htr3a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_5 cells by expression of Snx31. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Hippocampal region, in or close to the regions: Posterior amygdalar nucleus, Dentate gyrus, polymorph layer, Field CA3, pyramidal layer, Field CA3, stratum radiatum, Dentate gyrus, molecular layer, Dentate gyrus, granule cell layer. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:0699 RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_5 (CS20230722_CLUS_0699)." []
comment: Warning: This type RHP-COA Ndnf Gaba_5 Snx31 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for retrohippocampal region (RHP), cortical amygdalar area (COA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
