name: Sst Chodl Gaba_1 Adamts5 sst chodl GABAergic cortical interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A sst chodl GABAergic cortical interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm31218 (Mmus), Tshr (Mmus), Ecel1 (Mmus), Adamts5 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Sst Chodl Gaba_1 cells by expression of Adamts5, Tshr. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Striatum, Substantia innominata, Pallidum, Central amygdalar nucleus, lateral part, Globus pallidus, external segment, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part, Anterior amygdalar area, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:0845 Sst Chodl Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_0845)." []
