[Term]
id: PCL:0113296
name: NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_12 medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron (Mmus)
def: "A medial ganglionic eminence derived interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chrna2 (Mmus), Slc10a4 (Mmus), Sostdc1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba cells by expression of Tgfb2. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Striatum ventral region, Cortical subplate, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Striatum, Substantia innominata, Caudoputamen, Lateral preoptic area, Fundus of striatum, Central amygdalar nucleus, capsular part, Globus pallidus, external segment, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:0916 NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_12 (CS20230722_SUPT_0255, CS20230722_CLUS_0916)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, NDB-SI-MA-STRv Lhx8 Gaba_12 does not have cells in diagonal band nucleus (NDB), magnocellular nucleus (MA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
