id: PCL:0113568
name: MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_1 Egfr neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cplx3 (Mmus), Zan (Mmus), Npr3 (Mmus), Moxd1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Egfr, Moxd1. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate, in or close to the regions: Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Piriform-amygdalar area, Medial amygdalar nucleus, Basolateral amygdalar nucleus, ventral part, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part, Nucleus of the lateral olfactory tract, pyramidal layer. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1188 MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_1188)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_1 Egfr does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1188 MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_1" EXACT []
