[Term]
id: PCL:0113617
name: MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_10 Itpr3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tll2 (Mmus), Kcnmb1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_10 cells by expression of Itpr3. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Olfactory areas, Cortical subplate, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Pallidum, Cortical amygdalar area, anterior part, Medial amygdalar nucleus, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1237 MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_10 (CS20230722_CLUS_1237)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_10 Itpr3 does not have cells in bed nuclei of the stria terminalis (BST). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1237 MEA-BST Sox6 Gaba_10" EXACT []
synonym: "Tll2 (Mmus), Kcnmb1 (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
