[Term]
id: PCL:0113697
name: SI-MA-ACB Ebf1 Bnc2 Gaba_1 Sulf1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Bnc2 (Mmus), Dlx1 (Mmus), Bcl11b (Mmus), Asb4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SI-MA-ACB Ebf1 Bnc2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Sulf1, Myo3b. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Lateral septal complex, Striatum ventral region, Olfactory areas, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Striatum, Substantia innominata, Olfactory areas, Nucleus accumbens, Olfactory tubercle. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1317 SI-MA-ACB Ebf1 Bnc2 Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_1317)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, SI-MA-ACB Ebf1 Bnc2 Gaba_1 Sulf1 does not have cells in magnocellular nucleus (MA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1317 SI-MA-ACB Ebf1 Bnc2 Gaba_1" EXACT []
synonym: "Bnc2 (Mmus), Dlx1 (Mmus), Bcl11b (Mmus), Asb4 (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
