[Term]
id: PCL:0113731
name: CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1 Hmcn1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nts (Mmus), Six3 (Mmus), Hmcn1 (Mmus), Tmem215 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Hmcn1. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Intercalated amygdalar nucleus, Pallidum, Central amygdalar nucleus, capsular part, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1351 CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_1351)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1 Hmcn1 does not have cells in anterior amygdalar area (AAA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1351 CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1" EXACT []
synonym: "Nts (Mmus), Six3 (Mmus), Hmcn1 (Mmus), Tmem215 (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
