[Term]
id: PCL:0113732
name: CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1 Prok2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prok2 (Mmus), Slc5a7 (Mmus), Meis2 (Mmus), Slc32a1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Prok2, Slc5a7. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Substantia innominata, Basomedial amygdalar nucleus, anterior part, Pallidum, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Central amygdalar nucleus, capsular part, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1352 CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_1352)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1 Prok2 does not have cells in anterior amygdalar area (AAA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1352 CEA-AAA-BST Six3 Sp9 Gaba_1" EXACT []
synonym: "Prok2 (Mmus), Slc5a7 (Mmus), Meis2 (Mmus), Slc32a1 (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
