def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ifi27l2a (Mmus), Isl1 (Mmus), Fgf10 (Mmus), Meis2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Glra1, Fgf10. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Lateral septal complex, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1380 ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3 (CS20230722_CLUS_1380)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3 Glra1 does not have cells in nucleus accumbens (ACB), fundus of striatum (FS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
