[Term]
id: PCL:0113762
name: ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3 Mbnl3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc17a8 (Mmus), Mbnl3 (Mmus), Cntn6 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Mbnl3, Prok2, Nts. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Striatum ventral region, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Striatum, Substantia innominata, Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Nucleus accumbens. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1382 ACB-BST-FS D1 Gaba_3 (CS20230722_CLUS_1382)." []
