name: MPN-MPO-LPO Lhx6 Zfhx3 Gaba_1 Six3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lhx6 (Mmus), Six3 (Mmus), Crhbp (Mmus), Klhl4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MPN-MPO-LPO Lhx6 Zfhx3 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Six3, Gldn. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Hypothalamus, Lateral septal complex, Striatum-like amygdalar nuclei, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Medial preoptic area, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Hypothalamus, Central amygdalar nucleus, medial part, Lateral septal nucleus, ventral part, fiber tracts. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1483 MPN-MPO-LPO Lhx6 Zfhx3 Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_1483)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, MPN-MPO-LPO Lhx6 Zfhx3 Gaba_1 Six3 does not have cells in medial preoptic nucleus (MPN), lateral preoptic area (LPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1483 MPN-MPO-LPO Lhx6 Zfhx3 Gaba_1" EXACT []
