[Term]
id: PCL:0114111
name: ZI Pax6 Gaba_3 Chrnb3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Chrnb3 (Mmus), Sp8 (Mmus), Sfta3-ps (Mmus). It is distinguished from other ZI Pax6 Gaba_3 cells by expression of Chrnb3. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Globus pallidus, internal segment, internal capsule. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1731 ZI Pax6 Gaba_3 (CS20230722_CLUS_1731)." []
comment: Warning: This type ZI Pax6 Gaba_3 Chrnb3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for zona incerta (ZI). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1731 ZI Pax6 Gaba_3" EXACT []
