id: PCL:0114265
name: PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_1 Zic2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Map3k15 (Mmus), Nts (Mmus), Zic4 (Mmus), Penk (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Zic2, Cbln2. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Hypothalamus, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Striatum, Medial preoptic area, Ventrolateral preoptic nucleus, Diagonal band nucleus, Substantia innominata, Anteroventral preoptic nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:1885 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_1885)." []
comment: Warning: This type PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_1 Zic2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, preoptic part (PVpo), ventromedial preoptic nucleus (VMPO), medial preoptic nucleus (MPN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "1885 PVpo-VMPO-MPN Hmx2 Gaba_1" EXACT []
