[Term]
id: PCL:0114581
name: SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_8 Garem2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Dmrta2 (Mmus), Sh2d4b (Mmus), Tmem132d (Mmus), Cgnl1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_8 cells by expression of Garem2, Cgnl1. It is glutamatergic. These cells are are located in the Striatum ventral region, Pallidum, in or close to the regions: Hypothalamus, Substantia innominata, Bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, Nucleus accumbens. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:2201 SI-MA-LPO-LHA Skor1 Glut_8 (CS20230722_CLUS_2201)." []
