name: PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_1 Ptgfr neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Bsx (Mmus), Ptgfr (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_1 cells by expression of Ptgfr. It is glutamatergic. These cells are are located in the Hypothalamus, in or close to the regions: Hypothalamus, Dorsomedial nucleus of the hypothalamus, Posterior hypothalamic nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:2390 PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_2390)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_1 Ptgfr does not have cells in lateral hypothalamic area (LHA). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2390 PH-ant-LHA Otp Bsx Glut_1" EXACT []
synonym: "Bsx (Mmus), Ptgfr (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
