name: PRC-PAG Tcf7l2 Irx2 Glut_1 Tstd1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Defb1 (Mmus), Tstd1 (Mmus), Prox1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRC-PAG Tcf7l2 Irx2 Glut_1 cells by expression of Tstd1. It is glutamatergic. These cells are are located in the Midbrain, in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Midbrain, Nucleus of the posterior commissure, Periaqueductal gray. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:2897 PRC-PAG Tcf7l2 Irx2 Glut_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_2897)." []
