name: SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5 Popdc3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Pth2 (Mmus), Has2os (Mmus), Dlk1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5 cells by expression of Popdc3, Has2os, Dlk1. It is glutamatergic. These cells are are located in the Thalamus, in or close to the regions: Medial geniculate complex, ventral part, Parafascicular nucleus, Nucleus of reuniens, Subparafascicular area, Ventral posteromedial nucleus of the thalamus, parvicellular part, Midbrain. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:2973 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5 (CS20230722_CLUS_2973)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5 Popdc3 does not have cells in subparafascicular nucleus, magnocellular part (SPFm), subparafascicular nucleus, parvicellular part (SPFp), posterior limiting nucleus of the thalamus (POL), posterior intralaminar thalamic nucleus (PIL), posterior triangular thalamic nucleus (PoT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "2973 SPA-SPFm-SPFp-POL-PIL-PoT Sp9 Glut_5" EXACT []
synonym: "Pth2 (Mmus), Has2os (Mmus), Dlk1 (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
