id: PCL:0116217
name: SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1 Glis3 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxa2 (Mmus), Iqcf3 (Mmus), Pth2r (Mmus), Chrnb3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1 cells by expression of Glis3, Gm13986. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Hypothalamus, Midbrain, in or close to the regions: Periaqueductal gray, third ventricle, Midbrain, Supramammillary nucleus, Posterior hypothalamic nucleus, Hypothalamus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:3837 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_3837)." []
comment: Warning: This type SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1 Glis3 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for substantia nigra, compact part (SNc), ventral tegmental area (VTA), midbrain raphe nuclei (RAmb). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1 Glis3 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Dopa, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "3837 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_1" EXACT []
