def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a3 (Mmus), Postn (Mmus), Ebf3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_6 cells by expression of Postn. It is dopaminergic. These cells are are located in the Midbrain, in or close to the regions: Midbrain reticular nucleus, Midbrain, Substantia nigra, reticular part, Periaqueductal gray. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:3874 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_6 (CS20230722_CLUS_3874)." []
comment: Warning: This type SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_6 Postn does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for substantia nigra, compact part (SNc), ventral tegmental area (VTA), midbrain raphe nuclei (RAmb). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
