id: PCL:0116257
name: SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8 Tecrl neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Tecrl (Mmus), Ebf2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8 cells by expression of Tecrl. It is glutamatergic and GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Hypothalamus, Midbrain, in or close to the regions: Midbrain, Parasubthalamic nucleus, Ventral tegmental area, Posterior hypothalamic nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:3877 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8 (CS20230722_CLUS_3877)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8 Tecrl does not have cells in substantia nigra, compact part (SNc), midbrain raphe nuclei (RAmb). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8 Tecrl does not secrete the neurotransmitter Dopa, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "3877 SNc-VTA-RAmb Foxa1 Dopa_8" EXACT []
