[Term]
id: PCL:0116343
name: PB-SUT Tlx3 Lhx2 Glut_1 Il1rapl2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Lmx1b (Mmus), Lhx2 (Mmus), Irx3 (Mmus), Rorb (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PB-SUT Tlx3 Lhx2 Glut cells by expression of Il1rapl2. It is glutamatergic. These cells are are located in the Pons, in or close to the regions: Pons, Parabrachial nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:3963 PB-SUT Tlx3 Lhx2 Glut_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_3963)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, PB-SUT Tlx3 Lhx2 Glut_1 Il1rapl2 does not have cells in supratrigeminal nucleus (SUT). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
