id: PCL:0116928
name: NTS Dbh Glut_4 Calca neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Slc6a2 (Mmus), Chrnb3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS Dbh Glut_4 cells by expression of Calca. It is noradrenergic. These cells are are located in the Medulla, Pons, in or close to the regions: Pons, Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part, Medial vestibular nucleus, Subceruleus nucleus, Parabrachial nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4548 NTS Dbh Glut_4 (CS20230722_CLUS_4548)." []
comment: Warning: This type NTS Dbh Glut_4 Calca does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, NTS Dbh Glut_4 Calca does not secrete the neurotransmitter Glut, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
