name: CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2 Acvr1c neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Svep1 (Mmus), Cckar (Mmus), Pax5 (Mmus), Meis2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2 cells by expression of Acvr1c. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Midbrain, Pons, in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, Superior central nucleus raphe, Midbrain reticular nucleus, Pons, Dorsal tegmental nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4613 CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2 (CS20230722_CLUS_4613)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2 Acvr1c does not have cells in nucleus raphe pontis (RPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4613 CS-RPO Meis2 Gaba_2" EXACT []
synonym: "Svep1 (Mmus), Cckar (Mmus), Pax5 (Mmus), Meis2 (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
