[Term]
id: PCL:0117033
name: PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3 Kl neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gm4881 (Mmus), Chrna5 (Mmus), Npas1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of Kl, Gm4881. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Pons, in or close to the regions: Pontine reticular nucleus, Tegmental reticular nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4653 PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3 (CS20230722_CLUS_4653)." []
comment: Warning: This type PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3 Kl does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part (PRNc). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3 Kl does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "4653 PRNc Otp Gly-Gaba_3" EXACT []
synonym: "Gm4881 (Mmus), Chrna5 (Mmus), Npas1 (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
