name: NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1 Ntsr1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Gata2 (Mmus), Inka2 (Mmus), Ntsr1 (Mmus), Pde3a (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1 cells by expression of Ntsr1, Pde3a. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Pons, in or close to the regions: Pons, Tegmental reticular nucleus, Nucleus incertus, Pontine reticular nucleus, caudal part, Pontine central gray. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4719 NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_4719)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1 Ntsr1 does not have cells in nucleus raphe pontis (RPO). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4719 NI-RPO Gata3 Nr4a2 Gaba_1" EXACT []
synonym: "Gata2 (Mmus), Inka2 (Mmus), Ntsr1 (Mmus), Pde3a (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
