name: PSV Pax2 Gly-Gaba_1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Col27a1 (Mmus), Pax2 (Mmus), Dach2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PSV Pax2 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Ptprk. It is GABAergic and glycinergic. These cells are are located in the Pons, in or close to the regions: Medulla, Principal sensory nucleus of the trigeminal, spinal tract of the trigeminal nerve. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4808 PSV Pax2 Gly-Gaba_1 (CS20230722_SUPT_1078, CS20230722_CLUS_4808)." []
