id: PCL:0117194
name: PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 Moxd1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxd3 (Mmus), Moxd1 (Mmus), Pax8 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Moxd1. It is GABAergic and glycinergic. These cells are are located in the Medulla, in or close to the regions: Lateral reticular nucleus, magnocellular part, Inferior olivary complex, Gigantocellular reticular nucleus, Intermediate reticular nucleus, Medulla, Lateral reticular nucleus, parvicellular part, Paragigantocellular reticular nucleus, lateral part. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4814 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_4814)." []
comment: Warning: This type PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 Moxd1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus prepositus (PRP). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4814 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
