id: PCL:0117198
name: PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 Gbx2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Foxd3 (Mmus), Frem3 (Mmus), Hmcn1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Gbx2, Frem3. It is GABAergic and glycinergic. These cells are are located in the Medulla, in or close to the regions: Medial vestibular nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4818 PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_4818)." []
comment: Warning: This type PRP Otp Gly-Gaba_1 Gbx2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus prepositus (PRP). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
