[Term]
id: PCL:0117315
name: MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Anxa11 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Nccrp1 (Mmus), Sox14 (Mmus), Tfap2b (Mmus). It is distinguished from other MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Anxa11. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Medulla, Cerebellum, in or close to the regions: Cerebellum, Nucleus y, Infracerebellar nucleus, Vestibulocerebellar nucleus, Interposed nucleus, Superior vestibular nucleus, Medial vestibular nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4935 MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_4935)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Anxa11 does not have cells in spinal vestibular nucleus (SPIV), nucleus prepositus (PRP). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1 Anxa11 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "4935 MV-SPIV-PRP Dmbx1 Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
