name: PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_2 Adgrg2 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Prrxl1 (Mmus), Tnc (Mmus), Pax2 (Mmus), Adarb2 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_2 cells by expression of Adgrg2, Hoxa5. It is GABAergic and glycinergic. These cells are are located in the Medulla, in or close to the regions: Nodulus (X), External cuneate nucleus, Medulla, Cuneate nucleus, brain. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4987 PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_2 (CS20230722_CLUS_4987)." []
comment: Warning: This type PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_2 Adgrg2 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for parasolitary nucleus (PAS), medial vestibular nucleus (MV). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
synonym: "4987 PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_2" EXACT []
synonym: "Prrxl1 (Mmus), Tnc (Mmus), Pax2 (Mmus), Adarb2 (Mmus) expressing neuron of brain (Mus musculus)" EXACT []
