[Term]
id: PCL:0117368
name: PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_3 L3mbtl4 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Neurog2 (Mmus), Adamtsl3 (Mmus), Skor1 (Mmus), Tacr3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_3 cells by expression of L3mbtl4. It is GABAergic and glycinergic. These cells are are located in the Medulla, in or close to the regions: Intermediate reticular nucleus, Medial vestibular nucleus, Spinal nucleus of the trigeminal, interpolar part, Parvicellular reticular nucleus. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:4988 PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_3 (CS20230722_CLUS_4988)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, PAS-MV Ebf2 Gly-Gaba_3 L3mbtl4 does not have cells in parasolitary nucleus (PAS). This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme.
