[Term]
id: PCL:0117387
name: RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba_1 Msx1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Msx1 (Mmus), Crabp1 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Msx1. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Medulla, in or close to the regions: Medulla, Lateral reticular nucleus, magnocellular part. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:5007 RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_5007)." []
comment: Warning: This type RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba_1 Msx1 does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus raphe pallidus (RPA). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba_1 Msx1 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "5007 RPA Pax6 Hoxb5 Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
