[Term]
id: PCL:0117459
name: NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1 Clec14a neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Abcc9 (Mmus), Mymk (Mmus), Ret (Mmus), Sox9 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Clec14a, Sox9. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Medulla, in or close to the regions: Area postrema, Uvula (IX). Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:5079 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_5079)." []
comment: Warning: This type NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1 Clec14a does not have cells in any of the regions it is named for nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS), parvicellular reticular nucleus (PARN). The name merely indicates that it is a subtype of more general transcriptomic type that does. This assertion is based on data from registration to a reference standard common co-ordinate framework and parcelation scheme. Warning: Despite its name, NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1 Clec14a does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "5079 NTS-PARN Neurod2 Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
