[Term]
id: PCL:0117558
name: CB PLI Gly-Gaba_1 Cdh1 neuron (Mmus)
def: "A neuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Cdh1 (Mmus), Bhlhe22 (Mmus), Aldh1a3 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CB PLI Gly-Gaba_1 cells by expression of Cdh1, Pde10a. It is GABAergic. These cells are are located in the Cerebellum, in or close to the regions: Simple lobule, Crus 1, Crus 2, Lobule II, Nodulus (X), arbor vitae, Lobule III, Declive (VI). Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:5178 CB PLI Gly-Gaba_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_5178)." []
comment: Warning: Despite its name, CB PLI Gly-Gaba_1 Cdh1 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
synonym: "5178 CB PLI Gly-Gaba_1" EXACT []
