name: Tanycyte NN_2 Mylk3 alpha1-tanycyte (Mmus)
def: "A alpha1-tanycyte of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Dynlrb2 (Mmus), Mylk3 (Mmus), Sfta3-ps (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Tanycyte NN_2 cells by expression of Mylk3. It is glutamatergic. These cells are are located in the Hypothalamus, in or close to the regions: Periventricular hypothalamic nucleus, intermediate part. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:5245 Tanycyte NN_2 (CS20230722_CLUS_5245)." []
