[Term]
id: PCL:0117692
name: microglial cell (Mmus)
def: "A microglial cell of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of C1qa (Mmus), Tmem119 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other Immune cells by expression of C1qa, Tmem119. These cells are are located in the Hippocampal region, Olfactory areas, Striatum dorsal region, Midbrain, Isocortex, in or close to the regions: Caudoputamen. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:5312 Microglia NN_1 (CS20230722_SUBC_334, CS20230722_SUPT_1194, CS20230722_CLUS_5312)." []
