[Term]
id: PCL:0117693
name: BAM NN_1 Mrc1 border associated macrophage (Mmus)
def: "A border associated macrophage of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Mrc1 (Mmus), Pf4 (Mmus). It is distinguished from other BAM NN cells by expression of Mrc1, Pf4. These cells are are located in the Cerebellum, Pallidum, Midbrain, Isocortex, Pons, Medulla, in or close to the regions: Caudoputamen, arbor vitae. Standard transcriptomic reference data for this class can be found at https://purl.brain-bican.org/taxonomy/CCN20230722 in cluster:5313 BAM NN_1 (CS20230722_CLUS_5313)." []
synonym: "5313 BAM NN_1" EXACT []
